      "note": "Provisional machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first independent proposal. Initial las owns karma or deed once; the later that deed repeats this participant and remains unwrapped. The second and third Tibetan las attach to deed after occurs and deed before which respectively, as proved by occurrence offsets. skad cig gnyis par is the second instant recast as moment after, retained at phrase depth; gnyis par alone is not banked as after. zhig/zhig pa are cessation verbs here, not indefinite particles; misleading short HGM headword entries are not imported. ILL:1878 supplies a shorter Tibetan parallel with a different English rendering that supports the shared cessation/functioning reading only through brtsad pa'i. dngos por owns thing; the English explanation that can have any affect on anything stays unwrapped. The two med occurrences own no longer exists and no longer respectively. Temporal snga logs kyi bar du and final lan du are distributed recasts and omitted rather than falsely nulled. Supplied participants, articles and auxiliary frames remain unaligned."
